# Bartholomew Windows action companion -- example configuration.
#
# COPY THIS FILE, do not edit it in place. `install.ps1` copies it to
# `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Bartholomew\companion.env` and never overwrites an existing
# one.
#
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS A SECRET, AND NOTHING SECRET BELONGS IN IT IF YOU
# INTEND TO COMMIT IT. The credential header below is the one line that carries
# a secret; keep the real file outside any repository. `install.ps1` writes it
# with an ACL granting only your own account, and `diagnostics` prints header
# *names* only, never values.
#
# Every line is `NAME=value`. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.

# --- where Bartholomew is ------------------------------------------------------
# The Bartholomew API. Use https for anything that is not loopback; an exposed
# deployment refuses plaintext at the request boundary anyway.
BARTH_ACTION_BASE_URL=https://127.0.0.1:5173

# This machine's device id, as it is enrolled on the Bartholomew side. A
# mismatch produces a refusal and no action -- a visible failure rather than a
# misdirected one.
BARTH_ACTION_DEVICE_ID=desk-pc

# --- credentials ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Carried verbatim so the deployment's device resolver can verify this machine.
# The companion defines no authentication scheme of its own. With no resolver
# installed on the Bartholomew side -- the shipped default -- the action channel
# answers 401 and nothing is ever dispatched. That is correct; do not work
# around it.
#
# One header per line inside the value, `Name: value`.
#BARTH_ACTION_CREDENTIAL_HEADERS=X-Bartholomew-Device-Token: put-the-real-token-here

# --- what this machine may be asked to do --------------------------------------
# Absent means NONE. A companion that has not been told what it may do may do
# nothing, and still runs and reports that honestly.
#
# Comma-separated, or the single word `all`.
BARTH_ACTION_CAPABILITIES=windows.launch_app,windows.focus_window,windows.manage_window,windows.open_url,windows.open_path

# --- the three allowlists -------------------------------------------------------
# EMPTY MEANS NOTHING IS PERMITTED, never "everything is permitted". A
# deployment that forgot one can do nothing through it, which is a visible
# failure; the alternative would be a silent opening.

# Applications, one `key=absolute\path\to\app.exe` per line. A request names the
# KEY; it can never name a path, and there is nowhere in the wire format to put
# a command-line argument.
BARTH_ACTION_APP_ALLOWLIST=notepad=C:\Windows\System32\notepad.exe
    calc=C:\Windows\System32\calc.exe

# URL domains, comma-separated. Matched exactly or as a parent of a subdomain,
# on label boundaries -- `bank.com` does not match `notbank.com`.
BARTH_ACTION_URL_ALLOWLIST=docs.python.org,example.com

# Filesystem roots, separated by `;`. A path is fully resolved -- symbolic links
# followed -- before it is compared, and executables and scripts are refused
# even inside an allowed root.
BARTH_ACTION_PATH_ALLOWLIST=C:\Users\YourName\Documents;C:\Users\YourName\Downloads

# --- optional -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Whether a clipboard READ may carry the clipboard's text back to Bartholomew.
# OFF by default: with it off the content never leaves this machine and the
# result carries a digest, a length, and whether the secret detector fired.
# Turning it on is a deliberate decision; detected secrets are refused either
# way.
#BARTH_ACTION_CLIPBOARD_RETURN_CONTENT=0

# Where the companion keeps its executed-action ledger. This file is what stops
# a restarted companion from running an action a second time; if it becomes
# unreadable the companion REFUSES every non-repeatable action until you delete
# it deliberately.
#BARTH_ACTION_STATE_PATH=%LOCALAPPDATA%\Bartholomew\action-state.json

#BARTH_ACTION_POLL_SECONDS=10
#BARTH_ACTION_LEASE_BATCH=5
#BARTH_ACTION_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
